 wrong direction and many of the ones pointing in the right direction are missing. Just from a quick glance at this map:https://visiona.conectabalear.com/map/Thanks for this tho! Didn’t think of checking for cameras!replyv-mdev 16 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] Some of the webcams doesn't work, for example in Torreblanca, Castellón. I guess it's normalreplyaljgz 49 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Living in Vancouver, I traveled to Toronto to watch the Eclipse in 2024. We faced a nasty cloud, and had to drive hundreds of kilometers (hundreds of miles) to get a reasonably good view. On the drive back I decided that I'll travel for the one that's happening today, and here I am, in Sierra, with some cool people.Solar eclipses happen rarely enough, and frequently enough, to act as milestones in my life: I can review what happened since the previous one, and make a plan for the next one.They are some of the most magnificent natural phenomena, much more interesting than what's expected.The only other one that I got to see in perfect conditions was in my home town, Isfahan in 1999. I hope this one is perfectly clear again, and I have some resolutions for the next one.replygillesjacobs 25 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Cool, there is no check on the direction of the camera. Various camera's I checked do not seem to point in the direction of the sun during totality. It does filter candidate cameras down though.replyembedding-shape 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] This is great, can easily see what spots are overfilled with people or not :) I'm still thinking about where exactly I'll go to see it, was thinking Calafell or Vilanova as they're nearby and easily accessible, but probably half of Barcelona thinks the same so better to go a bit inland. Probably I'll end up just outside Lleida I think.Any more Spanish HNers (or temporary visitors) who are going to any specific places to see it? :)replyAl-Khwarizmi 51 minutes ago | parent | next [–] I'm from A Coruña so I should be able to just go down to the street, walk like 100 m and see it. I just hope clouds don't spoil the show (at the moment it's looking good, but here you never know).replyegesko 40 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] I'm in Valencia, planning to watch it from the beach.replyiancuandrei 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] I'll go somewhere around Bilbaoreplydavidricodias 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] Colmenar Viejo seems a great spot ;)replyembedding-shape 1 hour ago | root | parent | next [–] Only 7 hours away :D I'm in the Maresme area, so probably will end up between València and Tarragona on some mountain :) Thanks for the tip though, I'll forward it to my Madrid friends.replyhagen8 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] Mountains close to leon?replyLongwelwind 20 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Does anyone know if there will be any live feed of the earth viewed from space during the eclipse?replyHelloUsername 2 minutes ago | parent | next [–] Maybe here? https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rSvCuSQhC3wreplyck2 3 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Isn't there a big ship out there traveling between the cloudsSurprised they don't have a starlink uplinkreplyLawrenceKerr 59 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Doesn't seem like the best of weather now in Iceland, hopefully it clears up. Otherwise it would suck for the people who have planned the trip months if not years in advance only to get a clouded sky, but that's always the risk with astrotravel.replybenoliver999 56 minutes ago | parent | next [–] Surely the smart money is to go to Spainreplyembedding-shape 52 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] We do get cloudy days too sometimes :) Although today it is looking fairly sunny all over the place: https://i.imgur.com/4LK7xo8.pngreplyTornhoof 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] Sierra de Guadarrama - Puerto de Cotos https://www.infonieve.es/espacio-nordico/puerto-de-cotos/web... looks decent, different views, good weather.replyfxn 21 minutes ago | prev | next [–] On a Virgin cruise near Ibiza, getting ready for it before sunset. Anyone else in the cruise say hello!replyxanthine 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] Sorry for my ignorance, but can someone please explain what I'm looking at here?replymsdz 1 hour ago | parent | next [–] About five hours from now, the sections of Europe indicated on the map will experience a total solar eclipse, with other regions of the continent experiencing a partial one.The map shows feeds to watch it.replyembedding-shape 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] Today there is a eclipse, the map shows where the eclipse will be. In the path of the eclipse, there are also a ton of live webcams, and this map shows those and let you preview the webcams. Does it make sense now?replyrob74 1 hour ago | root | parent | next [–] Even more specifically, it will start off over Greenland, continue over western Iceland and then finish with the sunset in northeastern Spain and the Balearic Islands.replyvoidUpdate 52 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] If you pan to the right, it shows that it actually starts in a bit of russiareplyNKosmatos 51 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Thanks for posting this, most of us won’t be able to view the eclipse but having a few webcams really helps to get the feeling!Hoping to be able to see the great eclipse of 2027 live ;-)https://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/solar/2027-august-2replyrythmshifter 19 minutes ago | prev | next [–] I get \"access blocked, referer is required\" errors tiled all over the screenreplydolmen 19 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Don't bother looking at Iceland: weather is awful right now.replymatsemann 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] https://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/solar/2026-august-12Nice page showing where it will be, with times and visualizations for any point/city.replyrythmshifter 20 minutes ago | prev | next [–] I get access blocked errors all over the screenreplydorienh 22 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Sad to be in Singapore where eclipse is not visible!replyhno8a34nwn 29